---

This project's architecture was informed by two MIT-licensed projects, whose
approaches were ported and reimplemented locally (no code vendored):

  * mutonby/openshorts        - face tracking, "heavy tripod" camera smoothing,
                                the two-speaker stacked layout, and the
                                edit-decision-list effect planner
  * Anil-matcha/AI-Youtube-Shorts-Generator
                              - transcript-driven highlight ranking, 20-minute
                                chunking with overlap, and the >50%-overlap
                                dedupe rule

Speaker diarization uses sherpa-onnx with pyannote segmentation-3.0 and a
WeSpeaker embedding model. Those model files are downloaded by
download_models.py and remain under their own licenses; they are not
distributed with this project.

The face detector is MediaPipe BlazeFace (Apache-2.0). Rendering uses FFmpeg
(LGPL/GPL depending on the build) as an external program.
